# Intent: The other grid games use the animation layer. Memory Match cards flip (the width closes to the edge and opens on the other face over 240 ms, with a soft tick by row), a mismatched pair flips back, Mine Finder's opened cell and Hangman's pressed key pop (112 percent for 160 ms). The layer gets two more tween kinds, a flip and a pop, with their math in the pure core and its host test; nothing new is drawn as an object and the rules cores are untouched. A game never moves the head.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.game.start match: a tap turns the card over smoothly, a mismatch turns both back after about a second; mines: a tapped cell pops when it opens; hangman: a pressed key pops and turns green or red.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: none beyond SF72 (the tweens live in the Grid struct, 8 at most); a few hundred bytes of flash.

